The '''2026 Preston City Council election''' was held on 7 May 2026, alongside the [[2026 United Kingdom local elections|other local elections across the United Kingdom]] being held on the same day, to elect 16 of 48 members of [[Preston City Council]] in [[Lancashire]], [[England]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=mhclgpress |date=2026-02-16 |title=Update on May 2026 local authority elections – MHCLG in the Media |url=https://mhclgmedia.blog.gov.uk/2026/02/16/update-on-may-2026-local-authority-elections/ |access-date=2026-02-17 |website=mhclgmedia.blog.gov.uk |language=en}}</ref>

== Background ==
In [[2024 Preston City Council election|2024]], the [[Labour Party (UK)|Labour Party]] retained majority control of the council.<ref>{{Cite news |title=Preston result - Local Elections 2024 |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/election/2024/england/councils/E07000123 |access-date=2026-02-17 |work=BBC News |language=en-GB}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Coyle |first=Simon |date=2024-05-02 |title=Preston local council election 2024 results in full |url=https://www.manchestereveningnews.co.uk/news/uk-news/preston-local-council-election-2024-29000444 |access-date=2026-02-17 |website=Manchester Evening News |language=en}}</ref> In January 2026, the council asked for the election to be postponed pending local government reorganisation.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2026-01-31 |title=Lancashire local elections 2026: where and why they have been cancelled - and when you can now vote |url=https://www.lep.co.uk/news/politics/lancashire-local-elections-2026-preston-chorley-burnley-blackburn-with-darwen-pendle-hyndburn-local-government-reorganisation-5489124 |access-date=2026-02-17 |website=Lancashire Evening Post |language=en}}</ref> However it was rescheduled on 16 February 2026.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Elections 2026 |url=https://www.preston.gov.uk/article/2128/Elections-2026 |access-date=2026-02-17 |website=Preston City Council |language=en}}</ref>

