Changes 2024–2026:
*May 2024: [[David Borrow]] (Labour) resigns – by-election held July 2024<ref>{{cite news |last1=Beardsworth |first1=Luke |title=Prominent Preston City Council Labour councillor David Borrow resigns triggering by-election for Lea and Larches |url=https://www.blogpreston.co.uk/2024/05/prominent-preston-city-council-labour-councillor-david-borrow-resigns-triggering-by-election-for-lea-and-larches/ |access-date=25 March 2026 |work=Blog Preston |date=24 May 2024}}</ref>
*July 2024: Sean Little (Liberal Democrats) gains by-election from Labour<ref>{{cite web |title=Local Elections Archive Project — Lea and Larches Ward |url=https://www.andrewteale.me.uk/leap/ward/20170/#2024-07-04 |website=www.andrewteale.me.uk |access-date=25 March 2026}}</ref>
*March 2025: Carol Henshaw (Labour) suspended from party{{efn|name=Your|Some sources report that Carol Henshaw has joined [[Your Party (UK)|Your Party]]. However, she is listed by Preston City Council as an independent.}}<ref>{{cite news |last1=Faulkner |first1=Paul |title=Preston Labour councillor suspended after 'antisemitism' complaint |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cvg1k7d1g8go |access-date=25 March 2026 |work=BBC News |date=11 March 2025}}</ref>
*September 2025: 
**Robert Boswell (Labour) resigns – by-election held October 2025<ref>{{cite news |last1=Faulkner |first1=Paul |title=Veteran Preston councillor steps down for ‘personal reasons’ prompting by-election |url=https://www.lep.co.uk/news/politics/veteran-preston-councillor-steps-down-for-personal-reasons-prompting-by-election-5304270 |access-date=25 March 2026 |work=Lancashire Evening Post |date=5 September 2025 |language=en}}</ref>
**Stephen Thompson (Conservative) joins Reform<ref>{{cite news |last1=Faulkner |first1=Paul |title=Preston City Coucil's Conservative group leader defects to Reform |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cwy5y4q45q1o |access-date=25 March 2026 |work=BBC News |date=2 September 2025}}</ref>
*October 2025: 
**Ronan Hodgson (Liberal Democrats) gains by-election from Labour<ref>{{cite web |title=Local Elections Archive Project — Ashton Ward |url=https://www.andrewteale.me.uk/leap/ward/20161/#2025-10-16 |website=www.andrewteale.me.uk |access-date=25 March 2026}}</ref>
**Liz Atkins (Labour) leaves party to sit as an independent<ref>{{cite news |last1=Walker |first1=Ed |title=Ashton councillor Liz Atkins quits Preston Labour to sit as independent |url=https://www.blogpreston.co.uk/2025/10/ashton-councillor-liz-atkins-quits-preston-labour-to-sit-as-independent/ |access-date=25 March 2026 |work=Blog Preston |date=23 October 2025}}</ref>

